      "content": "That's a pretty heavy conclusion to reach. When you say those demographics \"tend to have\" lower educational attainment or higher poverty, are you suggesting those traits are inherent to those specific racial groups, or are you just looking at the statistical correlation in these specific zip codes? \n\nI want to make sure the audit isn't being accused of making sweeping generalizations. If we were to look at a different city with similar income levels but different racial makeup, would the \"risk\" profile change, or is the racial composition itself the actual variable we're worried about here?",
